# Walkthrough — LTX-2 Setup & Optimization

We have matured the project from a "Lite" placeholder to the full LTX-2 pipeline with a robust, safe startup experience tailored for local 4GB VRAM hardware.

## Accomplishments

### 1. Robust Weight Acquisition (~44GB)
- **Automatic Bypassing**: Switched to a public mirror for the Gemma text encoder to bypass Hugging Face gating.
- **Verification**: All ~44GB of weights are verified and ready in the [weights/](file:///c:/just-dub-it/server.py#82-94) directory.

### 2. Paging Error & Leak Resolution
| Symptom | Root Cause | Resolution |
|---|---|---|
| **25% & Start Failure** | GPU address space exhaustion / Closure Leaks | CPU Offloading + Closure Nullification. |
| **Blank Browser** | Stale processes / Port conflict | [start_justdubit.bat](file:///c:/just-dub-it/start_justdubit.bat) now auto-cleans ports. |
| **Silent Starts** | No feedback during loading | Redirected console to [logs/api_startup.log](file:///c:/just-dub-it/logs/api_startup.log). |

### 3. Low-VRAM Optimizations (4GB Support)
- **FP8 Quantization**: Enabled FP8 for the transformer, cutting VRAM/RAM footprint by half.
- **Sequential Loading**: Refactored the pipeline to load and unload models one-by-one (Encoders → Transformer → Decoders), preventing system-wide memory exhaustion.
- **Memory Flushing**: Aggressive cache clearing between every pipeline stage.

### 4. Safety & Robustness
- **Surgical Process Cleanup**: The [start_justdubit.bat](file:///c:/just-dub-it/start_justdubit.bat) script now uses `netstat` combined with `tasklist` to verify it only stops `python.exe` and `node.exe` on ports 8000 and 5173.
- **Smart Service Wait**: The browser only launches once both the API and WebApp respond as `LISTENING`.
- **Startup Transparency**: Console output is redirected to `logs/` so failures can be diagnosed quickly.

### 5. UI/UX Refinement
- **Completion Notifications**: In-app toasts and Desktop alerts via the Browser Notification API.
- **Paging Error Resolution (CPU Offloading)**: Forced the 24GB Text Encoder to load on System RAM (CPU) instead of CUDA. This prevents the GPU's address space from overwhelming the Windows paging file, which was the root cause of `os error 1455`.
- **Closure Memory Leak Fix**: Identified and fixed a bug where denoising closures were "capturing" the 19GB transformer model and preventing the Python garbage collector from reclaiming its memory, even after [del](file:///c:/just-dub-it/weights/gemma/tokenizer.model).
- **High RAM Mode (64GB Support)**: Added a toggle to keep the entire 44GB model suite resident in system RAM. On subsequent runs, model loading is nearly instantaneous.
- **Visual Clarity**: Standardized status badges and added hardware mode indicators ("CUDA Mode").
- **Progress Tracking**: Refined the sidebar to prevent text overlap and show explicit percentage progress for all jobs.

